# No AI slop (product)

All user-facing writing in this product — UI strings, generation prompts, Núcleo
content, chat replies, demos, and agent-authored copy — must follow
`.cursor/skills/no-ai-slop/SKILL.md` and `shared/noAiSlopWriting.ts`.

When writing or editing copy:

- Lead with the point. Cut throat-clearing and empty setup.
- Prefer concrete facts, numbers, and mechanisms over abstractions.
- Use active voice and direct verbs.
- Ban puffery, binary contrasts, colon reveals, faux-insight setups,
  weasel attribution, synonym cycling, dramatic fragments, and summary kickers
  (see the skill for the full list, including Spanish equivalents).
- Keep Núcleo’s adult, sober voice — never coachy, celebratory, or commercial.

Generation backends must keep `NO_AI_SLOP_WRITING_CONTRACT` in system/user
prompts. Do not reintroduce the AI-slop demo Núcleo.
